# Lessons, Do-Not-Repeat and Decision Log

`context/notes/<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>-<slug>.md` hosts dated, reusable
lessons, Do-Not-Repeat rules and user preferences; the Decision Log is the
existing ADR records under `context/decisions/`. Read this file when
recording a lesson, a preference, a "do not repeat" rule or a decision.

## Where things live

| Item | Where | Kind |
|---|---|---|
| Key learnings | `context/notes/` lessons note | `notes` |
| Do-Not-Repeat rules | same lessons note | `notes` |
| User preferences | same lessons note | `notes` |
| Decision log | `context/decisions/` ADR records | `decision` |

## Lessons note structure

A note dedicated to lessons uses `context: lessons` in the frontmatter
and dated entries in the body:

```markdown
---
kind: notes
summary: "<1-2 sentence summary — MANDATORY, index source>"
context: lessons
created: "<ISO 8601>"
project: <project>
---

## Key learnings

- [<YYYY-MM-DD>] (<confidence>) <the lesson, one line> — <why it matters>

## Do-Not-Repeat

- [<YYYY-MM-DD>] (<confidence>) <what not to do again> — <what to do instead>

## Preferences

- [<YYYY-MM-DD>] (<confidence>) <stable working style or explicit preference>
```

## Rules

- **No H1 title** — body starts at H2; see AGENTS.md (document conventions).
- **Reinforce, do not duplicate**: repeat a lesson by appending a new dated
  line to the existing note, never by creating a second note (dedup-before-write,
  see `notes.md`).
- **Confidence labels** add provenance when useful, using the standardized
  claim vocabulary verbatim: `(measured)` (verified),
  `(expected)` (written, not run), `(inferred)` (static
  analysis only). Omit the label when a plain fact suffices.
- A rule becomes a Do-Not-Repeat entry only when it bit more than once; keep
  the list short and actionable.
- Architecturally significant decisions belong in `context/decisions/`
  (ADR records), not in the lessons note; link the ADR from the lesson that
  motivated it.
- Tier: **medium** — see `context/architecture/stack.md` for the tier taxonomy.
